Ludwerk: a GPU device made on the adapter asked for by its name.

SDL chooses the adapter itself: Direct3D 12 the one DXGI ranks first for
performance or for low power, Vulkan the suitable device of the best type.
A machine with an integrated GPU and a discrete one could not be told which
to draw on, and the two drivers chose differently -- Direct3D 12 followed
Windows' per-app GPU preference and Vulkan always took the discrete card.
SDL_PROP_GPU_DEVICE_CREATE_ADAPTER_NAME_STRING names the adapter, or a part
of its name, compared ignoring case; Direct3D 12 takes the first hardware
adapter DXGI lists with it, Vulkan the first suitable device with it,
whatever its rank. When none has it, the device is made where it would have
been, and a warning says so.

